WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(audience clapping)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.480
- Now that you're in your second season,

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:04.570
have the Schmidt fans from New Girl,

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:06.380
have they accepted the new role?

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:07.213
The Neighborhood?

00:00:07.213 --> 00:00:08.175
- I hope so (chuckles)

00:00:08.175 --> 00:00:10.750
- I'm a fan of Schmidt,
so I love you in both.

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:11.583
I think it's awesome.
- No yeah,

00:00:11.583 --> 00:00:12.440
it's been really cool

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:15.710
you know there's still a lot of New Girl

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:18.000
and Schmidt fans and you'll
be walking down the street

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:18.833
and somebody will go, "Schmidt!"

00:00:18.833 --> 00:00:20.690
and you're like, oh my God, what happened.

00:00:20.690 --> 00:00:22.287
- It's the greatest cast.

00:00:22.287 --> 00:00:24.900
- Yeah It was such a wonderful experience

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:27.080
and I love when I get recognized for it.

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:28.660
I mean, I'm so grateful for it.

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:30.480
But now we have all these
people who are coming up to us

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:32.117
for The Neighborhood and they'll be like,

00:00:32.117 --> 00:00:32.980
"I love your show",

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:35.626
and I'll be like, "Which one?"

00:00:35.626 --> 00:00:37.558
- And then you sound like that guy.

00:00:37.558 --> 00:00:38.920
Which one I have so many shows.

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:41.833
- Well I know, but I'm
actually curious about it,

00:00:41.833 --> 00:00:43.610
because it's usually New Girl

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.520
and I'm like, I'm really
proud of this other one.

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:46.590
- Yeah, yeah.

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:48.080
I know, but it's funny cause now that

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:49.800
Netflix takes over everything so everybody

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:52.510
that hasn't seen, like
New Girl was on for years,

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:53.830
and they're just now starting.

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:55.610
- Well you can kind of guess

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:57.210
who's coming up to you for what show

00:00:57.210 --> 00:00:59.800
because you'll have some pinned out teen

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:01.040
who's like "I love your show"

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:03.030
and you're like did you
just watch all seven seasons

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:04.403
of New Girl in a weekend?
(audience laughs)

00:01:04.403 --> 00:01:05.236
- Like one weekend. (laughs)

00:01:05.236 --> 00:01:06.069
- Yeah and they're like,

00:01:06.069 --> 00:01:08.370
"yes and it was amazing,
when you and Winston..."

00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:09.580
and you're like all right man let's just

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:11.350
let's sit down, let's get a coffee,

00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:12.250
everything--
- [Kelly] Hash this out.

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:13.510
- Everything's gonna be fine,

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:14.343
you just need to breathe.

00:01:14.343 --> 00:01:16.390
- Yes, and have you heard
of The Neighborhood.

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:17.223
- That's right.

00:01:17.223 --> 00:01:18.230
But then you'll have people who will come

00:01:18.230 --> 00:01:21.497
and it's like, "man I love
the show, you and Cedric",

00:01:21.497 --> 00:01:22.330
and it's been a really,

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:24.873
this show is, it's on CBS,

00:01:25.910 --> 00:01:28.410
it's really more of a
family oriented show,

00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:30.170
and so you're having
conversations with people

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:31.240
who are like "yeah you
know we get the whole

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:32.580
family together, we watch the show,

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:34.270
it's got such a positive message",

00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:35.880
and we love doing the show.

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:37.330
- That's a great outlook.
- Thanks.

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:39.710
- So what kind of real
life neighbor are you,

00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:42.402
are you one that like, you
make friends or you hide?

00:01:42.402 --> 00:01:44.610
- I feel like I'm a nice neighbor

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:47.310
because I'm anticipating my kids

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:48.435
throwing something through--

00:01:48.435 --> 00:01:49.490
- [Kelly] (laughs) breaking.

00:01:49.490 --> 00:01:52.553
- A window of a neighbor of mine or like,

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:57.690
being like "we should
totally prank the neighbors".

00:01:57.690 --> 00:02:00.550
My kids saying this, like
that's an idea they would have.

00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:01.800
- I did this weird thing,

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:03.290
I'm owning this on national television

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:05.210
but whenever I was a
kid, me and my friend,

00:02:05.210 --> 00:02:08.112
I don't know why we did it
but we would make phone calls

00:02:08.112 --> 00:02:08.945
and we'd be like,

00:02:08.945 --> 00:02:11.324
"yeah we wanna go to,
have a flight to Jamaica,

00:02:11.324 --> 00:02:15.610
(fake laughs) yeah we need
to leave Tuesday the 16th",

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:17.380
we're like laughing and it's not funny,

00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:20.050
it's not funny, like it's not even funny,

00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:22.849
we were so stupid we weren't
even funny at our joke

00:02:22.849 --> 00:02:24.600
but we did it and we
thought we were hilarious.

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:26.395
- No I was like well what was the prank--

00:02:26.395 --> 00:02:27.947
- They're gonna think we're
coming to go to Jamaica.

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:30.863
- Yeah, what was the
prank and they'd be like,

00:02:32.247 --> 00:02:33.940
"we ordered a pizza" (Kelly laughs)

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:35.770
and you're like...

00:02:35.770 --> 00:02:36.690
- You rebel.

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:37.523
- Yeah I'm like this is,

00:02:37.523 --> 00:02:39.203
at least nail the bit.

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:43.500
- That's what I'm saying it
wasn't even funny (laughs).

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:45.410
All right well are you the dad who gets

00:02:45.410 --> 00:02:47.040
over involved, are you a helicopter dad?

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:48.910
Do you get overly involved?
- Uh.

00:02:48.910 --> 00:02:50.390
- That means yes, you hesitated.

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:52.920
- Yeah. (audience laughs)
- Yeah yeah.

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:54.770
Um, how do I answer this.

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:56.870
You are, you're afraid
they're gonna fall or,

00:02:56.870 --> 00:02:57.880
you're always kind of hovering?

00:02:57.880 --> 00:02:58.963
- I'm very like,

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:02.660
I've gotten over that to some extent,

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:04.660
I'm very please-y though,

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:07.264
meaning, so you know
it's Halloween coming up.

00:03:07.264 --> 00:03:08.097
- Yeah.

00:03:08.097 --> 00:03:10.160
- And so last year there was an incident

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:12.080
in which my daughter went to school

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:15.290
and her costume was Hermione
Granger from Harry Potter,

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:18.313
she was really excited, we
were excited, that's right.

00:03:19.162 --> 00:03:19.995
(audience laughs)

00:03:19.995 --> 00:03:21.110
- [Kelly] That's right she's cute.

00:03:21.110 --> 00:03:23.270
- So she was really excited
and she went to school

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:24.520
she did like the school parade

00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:26.170
and she came home and we had,

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:29.470
we live in a good neighborhood
for trick-or-treating

00:03:29.470 --> 00:03:31.870
and right before people
were gonna come over

00:03:31.870 --> 00:03:32.870
cause we were having some people over

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:34.570
we were all gonna go out together,

00:03:36.050 --> 00:03:37.970
I just hear a commotion in the other room,

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:40.380
and I can hear the tone is upset,

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:41.600
and I walk in I go, what's going on,

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:43.200
she's like I don't have my cape,

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:44.460
and I go why don't you just
throw on like a T-shirt

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:45.293
or something and she was like,

00:03:45.293 --> 00:03:48.267
"no, Hermione Granger is
nothing without her cape"

00:03:48.267 --> 00:03:49.100
(audience laughs)

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:49.933
and I go, well where is it,

00:03:49.933 --> 00:03:51.350
she goes, "I think I left it at school",

00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:55.150
I go (sighs), I'll go to the school.

00:03:55.150 --> 00:03:58.230
So I like get in the car,
I run over to the school,

00:03:58.230 --> 00:03:59.210
there's no cape,

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:01.710
and I call the house from the school phone

00:04:01.710 --> 00:04:03.490
and I'm like, where is it?

00:04:03.490 --> 00:04:06.310
And she's like "I don't know".

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:07.800
So I finally am like,

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:09.780
I don't know what to do I've
been here for 45 minutes,

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:10.710
I'm like leaving,

00:04:10.710 --> 00:04:13.470
I see in the corner of the schoolyard

00:04:13.470 --> 00:04:16.050
this bundled up black piece of cloth

00:04:16.050 --> 00:04:17.940
and I go, that can't be it,

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:21.915
and I run over and I pull
it up and I go, this idiot.

00:04:21.915 --> 00:04:24.490
(audience laughs)

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:27.330
And so I run to my car at
this point I'm sweating

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:29.420
I'm like barreling through traffic,

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:31.560
they're about to start to
go out to trick-or-treat,

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:33.530
I get home, I run through the door,

00:04:33.530 --> 00:04:35.260
Lily and all her friends
are running around

00:04:35.260 --> 00:04:36.140
I'm like, here's your cape,

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:37.340
and she's like "thanks Dad",

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:38.989
and then runs off.

00:04:38.989 --> 00:04:40.113
(audience laughs)

00:04:40.113 --> 00:04:42.920
- And that's why I would have
just given her the sheet.

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:43.753
They don't appreciate it.

00:04:43.753 --> 00:04:45.663
- And now I'm like hyperventilating,

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:47.960
I'm literally on the floor,

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:50.605
my wife walks by and goes
"where have you been?"

00:04:50.605 --> 00:04:53.438
(audience laughs)

00:04:55.638 --> 00:04:59.330
- Uh, just saving the day, you're welcome.

00:04:59.330 --> 00:05:01.350
Kids are like that though
you go above and beyond

00:05:01.350 --> 00:05:03.090
that's why I've learned just don't,

00:05:03.090 --> 00:05:03.923
just don't go above and beyond.

00:05:03.923 --> 00:05:04.899
- Yeah no, I know.

00:05:04.899 --> 00:05:05.800
You know what you gotta set them up

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:07.970
life will have disappointments
this is the first one,

00:05:07.970 --> 00:05:10.173
it's fine.
- I know, I know.

00:05:10.173 --> 00:05:13.170
- It's fine. You're such a good person.

00:05:13.170 --> 00:05:15.820
- I'm making up for a lot
of mistakes (Kelly laughs).

00:05:16.770 --> 00:05:18.560
- Okay do you help with
homework like all of that,

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:19.760
are you that kind of dad?

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:21.350
- Big time.
- Yeah?

00:05:21.350 --> 00:05:22.350
God you're so good.

00:05:22.350 --> 00:05:23.739
- There is a part of me that's like,

00:05:23.739 --> 00:05:26.240
we're getting into some
more stuff and I'm like,

00:05:26.240 --> 00:05:28.853
I wonder how I'm gonna do in fourth grade.

00:05:28.853 --> 00:05:29.686
- Dude.
- Do you know what I mean?

00:05:29.686 --> 00:05:30.519
- Yeah.

00:05:30.519 --> 00:05:32.247
- Like she'll get tests
back and she's like,

00:05:32.247 --> 00:05:33.970
"I got an 84" and I'm like,

00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:35.993
we got an 84.

00:05:35.993 --> 00:05:37.540
(audience laughs)

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:40.210
- This is why, I like
doing homework with them,

00:05:40.210 --> 00:05:42.060
but I feel like the older they get

00:05:42.060 --> 00:05:44.140
they just get lazy about it if
I'm sitting there with them.

00:05:44.140 --> 00:05:45.240
They'll be like, "oh I don't know",

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:46.550
I start getting the I don't know answer

00:05:46.550 --> 00:05:49.320
and I'm like I'm out, nope,
you're just being lazy.

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:51.653
- I try to read where they're at mentally,

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:53.570
I shouldn't say they're,

00:05:53.570 --> 00:05:55.520
our son's four he doesn't get homework.

00:05:57.767 --> 00:05:58.634
- [Kelly] (laughs) from Montessori.

00:05:58.634 --> 00:06:00.600
- If she's like wiped out,

00:06:00.600 --> 00:06:02.660
you know she does a lot
of after school stuff

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:03.590
she's on the basketball team

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:06.470
and I can see that
we're barely holding on,

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:07.840
let's sit down and do this together

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:08.938
and I'll walk you through it.

00:06:08.938 --> 00:06:09.771
- Yeah, I have my moments,

00:06:09.771 --> 00:06:11.580
but sometimes I'm like,
you're on your own dude.

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:12.413
- There's a lot of that.

00:06:12.413 --> 00:06:13.850
- I'm like you're just being lazy

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:15.790
and want me to do the problem
and I'm not gonna do it

00:06:15.790 --> 00:06:17.880
cause I don't know how to do fifth grade,

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:19.107
like I don't know how.

00:06:19.107 --> 00:06:19.940
(audience laughs)

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:20.773
So you're like whatever.

00:06:20.773 --> 00:06:23.913
Hope you nail it! (laughs)

